claim REDS 20260908.065244 -- diffuser reconciles the older transcript-naming obligation against its landed descendant; Bakery's runner implementation stays unchanged
obs Add a research file with a reproducible copied-source experiment and a design file defining request completion. The probe changes the hosted module's entry point, observes its bound socket, and compares delivered, withheld, and nonblocking receive calls.
obs The tree opened clean at f853fed32b with sixteen stashes. All thirteen added parked logs remain present. Five energy artifacts equal stash zero; the energy witness differs only by Grass's landed output-before-assert ordering at 002497bf0. Three topology artifacts equal stash eleven after the known underscore and spoken-hyphen rename substitutions. Preserve every stash.
obs Read the newest seat transcript and the day shelf's first three records. The seat transcript carries this running session; the previous completed diffuser log supplies its recommendation. Clockout and gates-only markers were absent.
obs Two detached launches ended before a completed receipt was available. A third kept a waiting shell alive, used the runner's returned transcript path, and finished with tree_moved=no. Its sixteen stash detail lines match git stash list exactly.
obs The prior recommendation already named the PATH requirement, and I missed applying it before the cold launch. The cold environment lacked installed ripgrep on PATH. Shell-dialect refused its forty-seven-behavior expectation; Amphora's disagreement plant failed to refuse; the roster summary then reported those two reds. Adding the installed ripgrep directory to this task's PATH makes both direct witnesses pass. No guard source changed.
obs The current standing-equipment witness passes its refusal controls. Its printed-path, header, elder-truncation, mode-separation, and append-shaped failing-side checks prove the repair already described by closed row 20260908.113404. The older row 20260908.065244 kept that remainder OPEN. Close it against the existing proof, without claiming that a tool can prevent every prompt-level misuse. The row stays on the living pin because the required fold witness remains gated.
obs A prepared fold was withheld when dated_path_witness counted 98 lost references against its ceiling of 85, with lost_promised_living=0. This is the existing gate at 20260908.082356. The full fold draft stays in session-output/query-wait-probe/held-fold.md; its checkpoint and recital edits were withdrawn before staging. A concise closure keeps the original row on the pin within 40960 bytes. No reference threshold changed.
obs The source checks build_response and encode_response before send. The copied recv_wire function accepts one loopback byte; withheld delivery leaves it running through the parent's 250 ms observation; the nonblocking control prints RecvFailed. The source reading identifies no local receive deadline. The experiment makes no claim about an outer supervisor or an infinite wait.
obs The parent starts its clock after a bound-port announcement, which precedes recvfrom. It sends TERM only to its own exact child after verifying that child's working directory. Port zero gives this experiment its own kernel-selected port. It sends no external traffic and runs no query or cryptographic exchange over the network.
obs Early control reads failed to capture the expected diagnostic. Explicit error reporting and unbuffered byte pipes produce a stable record; the final reproduction runs all three cases successfully. No production change was needed.
obs The design proposes a terminal outcome, absolute deadline, request identity, and reservation ownership. It distinguishes an empty success from refusal and requires a late reply to leave a reused slot unchanged. Bakery owns any implementation; Patchouli reviews the Tally seam. A caller's accepted deadline and concurrency remain unspecified, and storage planning stays conditional.
obs RFC 8085 section 3.3, published March 2017 and read 2026-09-09, supplies the external reliability background. The local experiment establishes no energy saving, storage performance, deployed deadline, or durable recovery.
obs After the cold pass, both pulls adopted 7d2e4d9b70. The receiver and runner sources used by this lap are unchanged from f853fed32b. The new session-roster rule and its guard remain as pulled. Naming rulings, incremental scrub, and seed publication keep their gates.
